<BaseLayout title="OpenIT — Terms">
  <h1>Terms</h1>
  <p class="lede">Last updated May 2026.</p>

  <h2>Open source software</h2>
  <p>
    OpenIT is released under the Apache License 2.0. You may use, modify, and
    distribute it under the terms of that license. See the
    <a href="https://github.com/openit-app/openit-app/blob/main/LICENSE">LICENSE</a>
    file for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Beta software</h2>
  <p>
    OpenIT is currently in public beta. Behavior changes between releases, and
    while we test before each release, things will break in your specific
    environment from time to time. Back up critical data.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    OpenIT is provided "as is," without warranty of any kind, express or
    implied. We don't accept liability for incidental or consequential damages
    arising from use of the software.
  </p>

  <h2>Use</h2>
  <p>
    You may install and run OpenIT for your organization's IT operations. Don't
    use the app to attack systems you don't own or have permission to test.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>
    OpenIT checks for updates on launch and offers to install them in-place.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@pinkfish.ai">hello@pinkfish.ai</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
